.el .ds Aq '
.TH setup 1  "setup " 
.SH NAME
setup \- Wire host\-specific agent integration (idempotent, merge\-only). `nxf init` stays tool\-agnostic; this opts a project into a host\*(Aqs deterministic delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsetup\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wire host\-specific agent integration (idempotent, merge\-only). `nxf init` stays tool\-agnostic; this opts a project into a host\*(Aqs deterministic delivery
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
setup\-claude(1)
Wire Claude Code: (re)assemble the shared agent file (AGENTS.md) and one SessionStart hook per active module (`nxf prime`, `nxm prime`, `nxc prime`) plus the `nxs`/module permission allowlist, merged into `.claude/settings.json` (idempotent, never overwriting). The canonical verb is `nxs setup claude`; this delegates to it (host setup is an umbrella responsibility)
.TP
setup\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
